Alembic migration environment for Plexive.

Start with backend/alembic.ini -- its header explains the rename hazard and why
there is no sqlalchemy.url in it.

Three things here are not stock and should not be "tidied" back:

  env.py            Reads app.database.DATABASE_URL rather than alembic.ini, so
                    there is one definition of where the database is. Announces
                    the resolved host before connecting. Refuses upgrade /
                    downgrade / stamp / merge unless PLEXIVE_DB_WRITE=1, and
                    fails closed when it cannot tell which command is running.

  policy.py         What counts as a difference: the deliberately unmanaged
                    tables, and the compare_type / compare_server_default /
                    include_schemas settings. Imported by env.py AND by
                    scripts/schema_diff.py so the two cannot drift apart.

  script.py.mako    Puts the review warnings at the top of every generated
                    migration, which is where somebody about to apply one will
                    actually read them.

To ask whether the live schema matches models.py, do NOT start with
`alembic check`: it requires the database to be at the head revision, so against
an unstamped database it exits 127 with "Target database is not up to date", and
it creates an empty alembic_version table on the way. Use the read-only report,
which works unstamped and writes nothing:

    .venv\Scripts\python.exe scripts\schema_diff.py

`alembic check` becomes the right tool once the database has been stamped.

Full reasoning, the interpretation guide for each kind of difference, and the
order the live commands must be run in: docs/research/schema-drift-2026-08.md
